From: Rex Lu <rex.lu@mediatek.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Sep 2024 14:17:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_wed: refactor mtk_wed_attach for support wed2

for mt7988d, pcie will bootup with pcie0 and pcie2.
pcie0 => wed0
pcie2 => wed2

Ported from MediaTek's mtk-openwrt-feeds
(commit d8194f5755013d6714eeb5454c522c72c0260536, "refactor
mtk_wed_attach for support wed2"). The upstream mtk_wed_attach()
unconditionally rejected any PCI domain > 1 via
pci_domain_nr(dev->wlan.pci_dev->bus) > 1, which prevented WED from
ever attaching on boards where hif2 sits on PCI domain 2 (dual-PCIe
"eagle + 7988d" topology, e.g. ASUS ZenWiFi BT8 / MT7988D). Also
collapses the AMSDU HIFTXD_SRC field to a binary 0/1 index instead of
using the raw hw->index, matching the same 3-domain topology.

Verified on ASUS ZenWiFi BT8 (MT7988D, hif on PCI domain 0, hif2 on
PCI domain 2): without this patch, insmod mt7996e.ko wed_enable=1
attaches wed0 successfully but silently fails to attach wed2 (blocked
by the domain check with the module falling into a broken half-WED
state on some paths). With this patch, both wed0 and wed2 attach
successfully and the device continues to operate normally with WED
enabled, confirmed via serial console across multiple reboots.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c	2026-08-23 13:13:10.609761011 +0300
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c	2026-08-22 15:50:27.193500675 +0300
@@ -618,7 +618,7 @@
 
 	/* init partial amsdu offload txd src */
 	wed_set(dev, MTK_WED_AMSDU_HIFTXD_CFG,
-		FIELD_PREP(MTK_WED_AMSDU_HIFTXD_SRC, dev->hw->index));
+		FIELD_PREP(MTK_WED_AMSDU_HIFTXD_SRC, (dev->hw->index ? 1: 0)));
 
 	/* init qmem */
 	wed_set(dev, MTK_WED_AMSDU_PSE, MTK_WED_AMSDU_PSE_RESET);
@@ -2411,9 +2411,7 @@
 	RCU_LOCKDEP_WARN(!rcu_read_lock_held(),
 			 "mtk_wed_attach without holding the RCU read lock");
 
-	if ((dev->wlan.bus_type == MTK_WED_BUS_PCIE &&
-	     pci_domain_nr(dev->wlan.pci_dev->bus) > 1) ||
-	    !try_module_get(THIS_MODULE))
+	if (!try_module_get(THIS_MODULE))
 		ret = -ENODEV;
 
 	rcu_read_unlock();
